Expectation and Variance of the Estimated Mean

Since we are taking an SRS within each stratum, stratum-specific estimates are unbiased: \[E(\bar{y}_h) = \bar{y}_{hU} \quad\quad\quad E(\hat{t}_h) = t_{hU} \quad\quad\quad E(\hat{p}_h) = p_{hU}\]
This implies that: \[\begin{flalign}
E(\bar{y}_{str}) &= E\left(\sum_{h=1}^H \frac{N_h}{N} \bar{y}_h \right) = &% \sum_{h=1}^H \frac{N_h}{N} E(\ybar_h) = \sum_{h=1}^H \frac{N_h}{N} \ybar_{hU}  = \ybar_U
\end{flalign}\]
Samples are taken independently in each stratum.
Remember that if \(X\) and \(Y\) are independent, \(V(X+Y) = V(X)+V(Y)\). Thus: \[\begin{flalign}
V(\bar{y}_{str}) &= V\left(\sum_{h=1}^H \frac{N_h}{N} \bar{y}_h \right) =&% = \sum_{h=1}^H V \left( \frac{N_h}{N} \ybar_h \right) = \sum_{h=1}^H \left(\frac{N_h}{N}\right)^2 V(\ybar_h) = \sum_{h=1}^H \left(\frac{N_h}{N}\right)^2 \fpchpar \frac{S_h^2}{n_h}
\end{flalign}\]

